 See the
 .Sx MOUSE SUPPORT
 section for details.
+.It Xo Ic mouse-hyperlink-hover
+.Op Ic on | off
+.Xc
+If on together with
+.Ic mouse ,
+request mouse movement events and show a pointing hand over hyperlinks while
+Control and Shift (without Meta) are held.
+The terminal must support OSC 22 CSS pointer names.
+This is off by default and does not change mouse key bindings.
+Hover feedback updates on movement between terminal cells, not on
+modifier-only key events.
+It is disabled in copy mode, command prompts, and overlays.
+The pointer is restored to an arrow when leaving a link and to text on detach.
